      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Under dry, oxygen-free argon using Schlenk/glovebox techniques, a toluene solution of (C5Me4SiMe3)Y(CH2SiMe3)2(THF) (0.793 g, 1.5 mmol) in a 300 mL Schlenk flask with a J. Young valve was frozen in liquid nitrogen, evacuated, and backfilled with H2. The mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 2 h; a second identical H2 charge was applied and stirring continued for 2 h. Solvent was removed under vacuum, the pale yellow residue was extracted with hexane and filtered, and slow evaporation precipitated 2. Single crystals were grown by recrystallization from hexane. Very pure dialkyl precursor is required for high yield.",
